{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1112646-what-s-a-fuckboy","id":1112646,"title":"What's a fuckboy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-07T06:50:03-07:00","id":1112646,"title":"What's a fuckboy?","content":"For real, I see this word everywhere, but I just don't quite get it. As a non-native speaker, it's hard to get all the nuance of relatively new words, so hit me with some context, y'all. I've seen it used in situations that can imply any if the following:<br /> <br /> Is a fuckboy 1) a boy who just wants to have sex with a girl, 2) a boy who just wants to have sex with a girl but pretends otherwise, or 3) a generally unpleasant boy?<br /> <br /> If a boy has sex with a girl who also just wants to have sex, is the term applicable to the boy?<br /> <br /> Is the term applicable for gays?<br /> <br /> Does the spelling &quot;fuccboi&quot; imply the same as the original spelling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 07-07-2017, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:15:42-07:00","id":1112659,"title":"","content":"Some US jargon-y synonyms for that particular word are &quot;douchebag&quot; or &quot;asshole&quot;; in all the contexts that I've heard it used here below the Mason-Dixon line have been derogatory without necessarily implying someone who wants sex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13636-blackaeon","name":"blackaeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13636_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T08:33:25-07:00","id":1112696,"title":"","content":"It's kind of a mix of all three. The term can refer to pretty much any unpleasant boy, but it does carry implications that he is unpleasant because he is immature and only interested in sex. A good way to think about it is that a fuckboy is <i>the kind of guy</i> who is only interested in sex (and will pretend otherwise if he thinks it will get him laid), whether or not he's currently pursuing sex. So, you might advise your friend, &quot;don't hang out with Nick, he's a total fuckboy&quot; not necessarily because Nick wants to have sex with your friend specifically, but because Nick's preoccupation with hooking up makes him unpleasent.<br /> <br /> It's also sometimes used to refer to a guy that someone wants to fuck, though in this case the implication is that sex is their only interest in the guy. For example, &quot;I need a quick bang, I'm gonna call that fuckboy Steve.&quot; Generally this communicates lack of respect for the boy, suggesting that sex is all he's good for.<br /> <br /> I've heard the term used both for straight and gay men, though much more commonly with straight men. And yes, the alternate spelling &quot;fuccboi&quot; means the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:07:38-07:00","id":1112719,"title":"","content":"In Florida, around the younger generation(teenagers) and among my Jamaican friends, a &quot;fuck boy&quot; is an &quot;insult&quot; synonymous with &quot;faggot.&quot; <br /> <br /> I hate the term, as it's extremely stupid and derogatory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T13:10:55-07:00","id":1112877,"title":"","content":"On the internet I've seen two main meanings:<br /> 1. A weak/submissive/beta/other synonyms person<br /> 2. A jokey form of address among the right crowd. Sort of like &quot;nigga&quot;. &quot;The right crowd&quot; are the operative words. Some communities consider this normal, others will ban you and call you names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T22:21:18-07:00","id":1113596,"title":"","content":"When I hear this term, I think of a young man who is promiscuous who is basically being used for sex or is just good for being used for sex. I think that there is an implication of homosexuality (likely because people tend to think that using somebody just for sex is more of a male thing, though plenty of women do it too) but not necessarily.<br /> <br /> I also find it to be pretty vulgar and disrespectful and it would likely make a bad impression on me if you to use this word except within certain narrow contexts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T15:36:30-07:00","id":1113902,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Throughout this discussion, please keep in mind that derogatory terms are, themselves, a sensitive subject for a large number of people.<br /> <br /> While we have no particular ban against discussing them, we do expect that care be taking in the discussion. Failure to be respectful on sensitive topics has caused many threads to be closed.<br /> <br /> If you need to reference a word that is similar to a racial slur to convey your point (n***a vs n***er), please be as explicit about your intent as possible.<br /> <br /> It never hurts to mask a portion of the words or clarify your intent to prevent misunderstanding.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b> Onyx Path Forum Moderator</b></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Read the rules</a><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is my mod voice.</span></b><br /> This is not my mod voice.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9-sparketh","name":"Sparketh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T06:05:29-07:00","id":1114127,"title":"","content":"3. I don't think it has anything to do with sex, but immaturity. Someone who is just &quot;Fucking around&quot; is not invested in accomplishing anything other than frustrating you. Once they've gotten maximal results for minimal efforts, they just flip the metaphorical table and laugh because nothing means anything to them. And a guy who spends all their time fucking around is a fuckboy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T22:14:51-07:00","id":1114436,"title":"","content":"I have seen it used in several ways, so I am uncertain. The most common use does seem to imply a derogatory term for a male who's seen a sexual object, rather than a complete person; similar to how the word&quot;Sl*t is used to describe a woman who is preoccupied with sex, or is perceived as only being good for sex. I AM confident that the &quot;boi&quot; spelling of boy is typically reserved for homosexual males.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T04:51:06-07:00","id":1114526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1112646-what-s-a-fuckboy?p=1114436#post1114436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I AM confident that the &quot;boi&quot; spelling of boy is typically reserved for homosexual males.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only within the LGBT community (and even then not specifically for males). Outside of it this <i>meaning </i>of the misspelling is practically unknown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T17:47:17-07:00","id":1114830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1112646-what-s-a-fuckboy?p=1114526#post1114526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only within the LGBT community</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> As someone who's around hundreds of teenagers and young adults every single day, I can assure you that the &quot;only&quot; part would be false. While I don't doubt people in the LGBT community use that spelling, it is definitely not restricted to the LGBT community.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T18:05:08-07:00","id":1114836,"title":"","content":"The word just means trifling fool but dialed up to Fwird status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T22:14:23-07:00","id":1114921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1112646-what-s-a-fuckboy?p=1114830#post1114830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> As someone who's around hundreds of teenagers and young adults every single day, I can assure you that the &amp;quot;only&amp;quot; part would be false. While I don't doubt people in the LGBT community use that spelling, it is definitely not restricted to the LGBT community.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read again. Spelling is used by everyone. Meanings are different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T22:32:40-07:00","id":1114930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1112646-what-s-a-fuckboy?p=1114921#post1114921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Read again. Spelling is used by everyone. Meanings are different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have only seen that spelling used in conjunction with that meaning. To me, that implies that 'boi&quot; has a specific meaning no matter who uses it, and I have only seen it used to refer to a male who bottoms. To be specific, I have seen the term &quot;cat-boi&quot; used to describe an effeminate male in feline-themed fetish-gear. I wish I didn't know that. No judgement if you're into that, I just didn't need the mental image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T05:07:43-07:00","id":1115032,"title":"","content":"Boi is just something people add to include an extra layer of dismissiveness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T08:53:50-07:00","id":1115104,"title":"","content":"Nevermind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T10:00:42-07:00","id":1115130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1112646-what-s-a-fuckboy?p=1115032#post1115032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boi is just something people add to include an extra layer of dismissiveness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or to just spell things as kewl as possible. For instance, Avril Lavigne's Sk8er Boi, which is about a heterosexual would-be romance.<br /> <br /> The word came up in an article I read, I think my first exposure to the word outside of the Jamaican culture decades ago, looking it up seemed to suggest the definitions in the thread are pretty spot on. Perhaps 'boi' is used in the LGBT community to mean homosexual males but I'm just as sure that they spell it with a y too and it could just be an extension of the dismissive or stylish element used outside of the LGBT community.<br /> <br /> Here's the part of the article that made me look it up back then.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].g