quot;boy&quot;. Either the way, I didn't care for the &quot;i&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T11:40:09-07:00","id":1115159,"title":"","content":"This thread is so bizarre. The only definition I've ever used or heard for fuckboy is that of an entitled jerk, the sort of guy you'd see studying business in some fraternity for rich kids. <br /> <br /> And the whole &quot;boi&quot; means something else thing is absurd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T13:14:46-07:00","id":1115216,"title":"","content":"Very interesting perspectives. I am somewhat relieved that my confusion isn't mine alone. \ud83d\ude0c<br /> <br /> Follow-up question: has any of you heard of someone using the word about themselves, either in a positive or self-disparaging way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T20:48:52-08:00","id":1175671,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The way I heard it being used, I was under the impression it refers to a male &quot;side piece.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Basically, if a girl is already in a relationship and has casual sex with you anyways, then you're a fuckboy</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1112646-what-s-a-fuckboy?p=1115032#post1115032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boi is just something people add to include an extra layer of dismissiveness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen the term <b>&quot;boi&quot;</b> used a lot among the furry community, which I've been part of for nearly half my life.<br /> <br /> The spelling B-O-I typically refers to effeminate males, particularly those resembling transgenders. Replacing the Y with an I is supposed to somehow mix the word Boy and Girl together.<br /> <br /> Doesn't make much sense when you think about it, but that's how it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-12-2018, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","cou